  null control: no ceiling sample: observed=(1.5, None) engaged=False planned=None high=None effective_max_kw=None
  store-only, twelve samples on an otherwise empty window:
    observed=None engaged=False planned=None effective_max_kw=None (no accessor reaches a store)

## B2: the latch under incremental evaluation (sticky, after every append)
  48 ceiling samples first on an empty window: engaged at append 48, final share 0.1429 at 336
  48 ceiling samples last on a full window: engaged at append None
  static shares only (they never decide the latch): 48/336=0.1429 48/192=0.2500 48/193=0.2487

## B3: the design's spike -- a second deque, no window write
  eleven ceiling samples: learned_max_kw=None observed=None engaged=False
  twelve: learned_max_kw=3.0 observed=None engaged=False
  48 ceiling samples in the store: learned_max_kw=3.0 engaged=False observed=None effective_max_kw=None
  lapse control: at day 46 -> None
  agree control: twelve at 4.5 kW (90% of configured) -> None
  MIN_SAMPLES still gates the window: 48 running samples; the store needs 12
